# .gitignore
# Use this file to tell git which files or directories to ignore (not track).
# About ignoring files:
# - Ignore OS and editor temporary files (e.g. .DS_Store, Thumbs.db).
# - Ignore virtual environments, build artifacts, and dependencies (e.g. node_modules/).
# - Large dataset files should be stored via Git LFS or external hosting; do NOT blindly
#   add large dataset files here if you intend to version them with Git LFS.
# - Lines starting with '#' are comments. Use a leading '/' to match paths relative to repo root.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Windows
Thumbs.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.env
venv/
.env/

# R / RStudio
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# Node
node_modules/

# Logs and temp files
*.log
tmp/
temp/

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/

# Build/dist
dist/
build/
*.egg

# Archives and packages
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar

# Data files
# If you want to ignore dataset files (not version them), uncomment the following lines.
# data/*.csv
# data/*.xlsx

# Note about Excel files and Git LFS:
# If you intend to track large .xlsx files in this repo, use Git LFS instead of ignoring them.
